# Docker build context = repo root (deploy/docker-compose.yml sets `context: ..`).
#
# CRITICAL: never let host-installed dependencies leak into the image. The
# Dockerfile does `COPY <ws>/package*.json` -> clean `npm ci` -> `COPY <ws>/ ./`.
# That second COPY would otherwise overwrite the freshly-pinned node_modules with
# whatever tree the checkout happens to carry. A stale @types/express-serve-static-core
# that way retyped req.query/req.params as `string | string[]` and broke `tsc` on
# prod while stage (clean tree) built fine — the classic "identical lockfile,
# different result" bug. Excluding node_modules makes the build reproducible.
**/node_modules

# Build outputs + generated code are produced inside the image, not copied in.
**/dist
backend/src/generated

# VCS metadata and local noise the build never needs.
.git
.gitignore
**/*.log

# Never bake env files / secrets into the image (mounted at runtime instead).
**/.env
**/.env.*
